id: ops-global-update-operands
title: Global npm update guard mistakes comment words and redirect targets for packages
description: "Follow-up to PR #289 thread PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64Vsn1: npm update -g # refresh and npm update -g >/dev/null currently return no findings. Round AN only changes continuation splitting. A separate line-based operand policy must handle comments and redirections while preserving approved fixtures. Companion finding in PR #206 also covers option values."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: follow-up,"gh:unbraind/pm-ops#289"
created_at: "2026-11-17T08:44:29.719Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T09:04:22.609Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-17T09:04:17.872Z",codex-sol,"Round AP fixing commit 54ddf53d91ed5daf31b9d4fb374e9affa0feff9d: every global update/up/upgrade/udpate is rejected without operand classification. New rejected fixtures: npm update -g --cache /tmp/x; npm update -g > update.log; npm update -g # nightly; npm up -g some-package; NPM_CONFIG_GLOBAL=true npm update. Added alias matrix across global markers and effective global/location environment scopes. Required package gates passed; all prior fixtures and real workflows pass. Left for orchestrator verification."
